              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "canō is inherited, usually traced to Proto-Indo-European keh2n-, \"to sing\" (EtymDB 2.1). English hen, the \"singing\" bird, is a distant cousin, and English chant comes from canō itself."
            }
          ]
